c Exactly one of variables 1 and 2 must be true.
c The first clause requires at least one to be true.
c The second clause prevents both from being true.
c A negative integer means NOT; each 0 ends a clause.
c The header declares 2 variables and 2 clauses. (P \/ Q) /\ (P \/ Q)
p cnf 2 2
1 2 0
-1 -2 0
